WEBVTT

00:02:00.170 --> 00:02:04.130
Do you read me?

00:02:06.410 --> 00:02:10.160
On the sixth day after starting their investigation of the ruins...

00:02:10.500 --> 00:02:17.250
...Adam regained a memory and they found a cockpit, proof that the ruins were a space ship.

00:02:18.190 --> 00:02:22.090
But the vital gravity control unit was broken...

00:02:22.240 --> 00:02:26.030
...and realizing that it couldn't fly, everyone became crestfallen.

00:02:27.150 --> 00:02:30.110
What do you mean? So it's hopeless?

00:02:30.640 --> 00:02:33.450
Just then, an earthquake began...

00:02:36.260 --> 00:02:37.580
What, what?

00:02:40.910 --> 00:02:42.150
Has it settled down?

00:02:49.580 --> 00:02:53.780
This is the Orion. [garbled] This [garbled]. Please reply.

00:02:53.890 --> 00:02:55.310
We picked up your distress signal.

00:03:02.630 --> 00:03:05.780
This is the Orion. We picked up your distress signal.

00:03:11.060 --> 00:03:13.500
Hello? Hello, can you hear me?

00:03:13.840 --> 00:03:14.700
Hello?

00:03:15.640 --> 00:03:16.460
Loud and clear.

00:03:18.300 --> 00:03:19.130
Hello?

00:03:19.580 --> 00:03:20.360
Move it!

00:03:20.660 --> 00:03:21.750
Please save us!

00:03:21.860 --> 00:03:22.800
It's terrible!

00:03:22.990 --> 00:03:23.960
We made an emergency landing...

00:03:24.300 --> 00:03:25.650
...there was nothing here...

00:03:26.030 --> 00:03:28.840
...whatever! Anyway, hurry and and get here!

00:03:28.840 --> 00:03:30.940
Howard, you're not helping.

00:03:31.130 --> 00:03:33.150
Let's leave this to Shingo.

00:03:38.930 --> 00:03:39.940
Hello?

00:03:40.130 --> 00:03:43.690
We're students of Soria Academy in Roca A-2.

00:03:44.210 --> 00:03:49.350
During our school trip, we were swallowed by a gravity storm and made a landing on this planet.

00:03:50.810 --> 00:03:53.930
Tell us your current situation.

00:03:54.450 --> 00:03:55.880
Nobody is injured.

00:03:58.690 --> 00:04:02.780
I'll give a detailed explanation later, but all together we're eight people and one animal.

00:04:03.710 --> 00:04:04.610
I'm a person!

00:04:05.140 --> 00:04:06.040
What about a space ship?

00:04:06.230 --> 00:04:07.160
We have one.

00:04:07.800 --> 00:04:11.590
But its gravity control unit is broken, so it won't fly.

00:04:11.930 --> 00:04:13.760
Is your Gyrostabilizer okay?

00:04:14.060 --> 00:04:14.740
Yes!

00:04:15.260 --> 00:04:16.010
Roger.

00:04:16.990 --> 00:04:18.300
We're heading your way.

00:04:20.630 --> 00:04:22.130
Um, what's your position?

00:04:22.460 --> 00:04:23.930
Are you already nearby?

00:04:24.230 --> 00:04:26.030
When will you come help us?

00:04:26.060 --> 00:04:28.310
Hello? Hello?! Hello!

00:04:28.760 --> 00:04:29.700
What happened?

00:04:30.300 --> 00:04:31.090
It cut out.

00:04:33.260 --> 00:04:34.730
Hello? Answer me!

00:04:34.910 --> 00:04:35.660
Hello?

00:04:46.730 --> 00:04:48.450
Why did it cut out?

00:04:48.450 --> 00:04:50.180
How would I know that?

00:04:50.700 --> 00:04:54.450
Maybe it cut out 'cuz they entered the atmosphere.

00:04:55.390 --> 00:04:56.440
That might be.

00:04:57.080 --> 00:04:59.740
They said they'd head our way, didn't they?

00:04:59.930 --> 00:05:03.900
Then help will really... really come, won't it?

00:05:04.730 --> 00:05:07.010
That's right! We can go home!

00:05:07.010 --> 00:05:09.040
Woo-hoo!

00:05:09.040 --> 00:05:10.390
We can go home!

00:05:16.390 --> 00:05:18.190
It's still too soon to be so carefree.

00:05:20.780 --> 00:05:23.930
Remember what happened when we entered the atmosphere.

00:05:24.750 --> 00:05:27.530
We got swallowed in an awful storm.

00:05:27.790 --> 00:05:30.190
We were struck by lightning and the shuttle was damaged.

00:05:30.490 --> 00:05:31.430
If...

00:05:31.950 --> 00:05:34.240
If that happened to the rescue ship...

00:05:34.580 --> 00:05:39.190
...and it were destroyed, then we wouldn't be able to get off this island the rest of our lives!

00:05:40.800 --> 00:05:46.130
It's okay. Kaoru's just saying not to get in high spirits too soon.

00:05:46.650 --> 00:05:47.360
That's right.

00:05:47.810 --> 00:05:51.600
Before the rescue ship gets here, we'd best do everything we can.

00:05:51.830 --> 00:05:53.030
Everything?

00:05:53.810 --> 00:05:59.810
First, I want to confirm whether the people coming to help us know where we are.

00:06:00.530 --> 00:06:05.250
I think they could figure out our exact position if they picked up our distress signal...

00:06:05.740 --> 00:06:11.660
...but the fact that their transmission cut out means their radar system may be useless.

00:06:12.000 --> 00:06:13.910
Well, in the worst case...

00:06:14.740 --> 00:06:18.110
We need to let them know where we are.

00:06:19.690 --> 00:06:21.600
That's better than waiting quietly.

00:06:22.240 --> 00:06:23.740
But how?

00:06:32.480 --> 00:06:33.600
A signal fire.

00:06:33.600 --> 00:06:36.410
It may be primitive, but this's the best way.

00:06:37.800 --> 00:06:39.190
But it's still not enough.

00:06:39.450 --> 00:06:40.650
What's not?

00:06:41.330 --> 00:06:44.810
We don't know which side of the island the rescue ship will come from.

00:06:45.110 --> 00:06:49.350
Yes... let's set up a signal at the north, east, south, and west of the island, and wait.

00:06:49.350 --> 00:06:51.190
What a pain.

00:06:51.380 --> 00:06:53.190
I'll stay here.

00:06:53.890 --> 00:06:58.130
We don't know when the rescue ship will try to contact us again, after all.

00:06:58.130 --> 00:07:00.750
What'cha sayin', pants-on-fire?

00:07:01.310 --> 00:07:02.330
What?

00:07:02.440 --> 00:07:09.190
Shingo's been sittin' in front of the communicator for <i>ages</i> for that exact reason!

00:07:13.690 --> 00:07:16.280
If you receive this transmission, please reply.

00:07:16.610 --> 00:07:17.510
Please reply!

00:07:18.230 --> 00:07:19.760
You get it?

00:07:22.010 --> 00:07:23.850
Chako, thanks.

00:07:23.960 --> 00:07:24.900
No biggie.

00:07:25.690 --> 00:07:30.750
Anyways, Howard, you get the closest one--the eastern end.

00:07:31.990 --> 00:07:33.680
Fine, I get it.

00:07:34.280 --> 00:07:36.000
I'll go to the west.

00:07:36.940 --> 00:07:38.480
Then I'll go south.

00:07:39.110 --> 00:07:41.180
Bell, please go with Menori.

00:07:41.290 --> 00:07:41.890
Okay.

00:07:42.410 --> 00:07:44.440
Sharla, come with me to the north.

00:07:45.000 --> 00:07:48.410
Chako and Adam, stay behind and keep Shingo company.

00:07:49.130 --> 00:07:49.950
Okay!

00:07:53.180 --> 00:07:54.380
You're going home?

00:07:55.880 --> 00:07:56.660
What's wrong?

00:07:57.190 --> 00:07:59.700
When your rescue ship comes, you're all going home?

00:08:00.230 --> 00:08:01.690
Yes, that's right.

00:08:02.180 --> 00:08:03.640
Will you leave me behind?

00:08:05.330 --> 00:08:08.210
Are you all going to go home and leave me behind?

00:08:08.400 --> 00:08:10.210
Of course not!

00:08:14.960 --> 00:08:19.390
Adam, you'll come with us. You can come home to our colony.

00:08:19.910 --> 00:08:21.490
So don't worry.

00:08:22.090 --> 00:08:25.760
We'd never leave you behind on your own.

00:08:28.990 --> 00:08:30.490
We'll <i>always</i> be together.

00:08:53.630 --> 00:08:55.240
It looks like it's going to rain.

00:08:56.440 --> 00:08:57.150
Let's hurry.

00:08:59.400 --> 00:09:02.030
Be careful--the wind is strong!

00:09:02.140 --> 00:09:02.890
Okay.

00:09:14.100 --> 00:09:15.830
Bell, take care of this.

00:09:16.310 --> 00:09:17.930
Where are you going, Kaoru?

00:09:18.410 --> 00:09:19.580
I'm just going to check something out.

00:09:28.760 --> 00:09:29.630
This is...

00:09:45.860 --> 00:09:47.210
There's a wind...

00:09:57.300 --> 00:09:58.160
Thanks.

00:10:05.210 --> 00:10:06.040
Kaoru!

00:10:06.600 --> 00:10:07.760
But how?

00:10:08.930 --> 00:10:11.210
I found a cave where we can climb up from below.

00:10:16.580 --> 00:10:20.810
If you go along the cliff and behind the waterfall there's a small cave!

00:10:21.000 --> 00:10:23.360
Go in there and climb up!

00:10:23.850 --> 00:10:25.130
Okay!

00:10:25.580 --> 00:10:26.330
Let's go.

00:10:34.280 --> 00:10:36.640
Who'd have thought there'd be a cave like this?

00:10:37.580 --> 00:10:42.680
Maybe the cave Pague went through when he was little was this one.

00:10:42.680 --> 00:10:48.380
More importantly, now we don't need to climb up that scary cliff any more.

00:10:49.650 --> 00:10:51.040
It's ironic.

00:10:51.860 --> 00:10:58.200
We finally find a convenient route right when we're about to be rescued.

00:11:07.650 --> 00:11:10.950
So the end of the eastern woods was like this...

00:11:29.510 --> 00:11:30.900
That startled me!

00:11:35.740 --> 00:11:37.610
Maybe I should go home...

00:11:43.610 --> 00:11:46.240
The weather looks kinda threatenin'.

00:11:46.430 --> 00:11:49.090
I wonder if everyone's okay.

00:11:53.630 --> 00:11:55.800
Let's confirm it one more time.

00:11:56.100 --> 00:12:00.600
Once we each get into position, we start the signal and wait there.

00:12:00.830 --> 00:12:04.540
If you see the rescue ship, give the sign and meet at Everyone's House.

00:12:04.950 --> 00:12:06.900
Well, everyone, take care!

00:12:14.930 --> 00:12:16.950
So, which way will it come from?

00:12:31.130 --> 00:12:34.280
C'mon, hurry up and rescue us!

00:12:43.130 --> 00:12:44.590
What should we do?

00:12:45.750 --> 00:12:47.590
It's really comin' down out there!

00:12:50.330 --> 00:12:50.930
How is it?

00:12:53.100 --> 00:12:54.680
No response at all.

00:12:55.240 --> 00:12:56.810
I wonder what happened.

00:12:56.960 --> 00:13:01.460
I feel like they were just trickin' us to get our hopes up.

00:13:01.760 --> 00:13:04.390
Maybe they had some kind of trouble after all.

00:13:04.840 --> 00:13:09.000
If they had a failure enterin' the atmosphere, the ship'd burn up.

00:13:09.000 --> 00:13:10.540
Quit it, that's not funny.

00:13:39.750 --> 00:13:40.760
What's up?

00:13:41.360 --> 00:13:43.430
The radar's picked something up.

00:13:43.910 --> 00:13:44.960
Something?

00:13:45.040 --> 00:13:46.840
It's obviously the rescue ship.

00:13:47.780 --> 00:13:49.390
Chako, watch the communicator.

00:13:49.650 --> 00:13:51.790
I wanna go see too!

00:13:52.610 --> 00:13:53.850
Even Adam...

00:13:54.750 --> 00:13:55.730
Do what'cha want!

00:13:57.560 --> 00:14:00.000
It feels like the rain is digging into my head.

00:14:01.280 --> 00:14:03.860
That's it, I quit! I'm going home!

00:14:11.030 --> 00:14:12.260
Hey!

00:14:12.260 --> 00:14:15.000
Hey, I'm right here! Hey!

00:14:17.810 --> 00:14:18.980
East is...

00:14:20.810 --> 00:14:22.910
This way! Come on, come on!

00:14:28.580 --> 00:14:30.040
Are you okay, Sharla?

00:14:40.310 --> 00:14:41.590
Get the signal ready.

00:14:42.490 --> 00:14:44.330
If we start now, we won't make it in time.

00:15:05.590 --> 00:15:06.750
Right here!

00:15:07.240 --> 00:15:08.700
Hey!

00:15:08.740 --> 00:15:10.160
Hey!

00:15:10.610 --> 00:15:13.760
Crap! I'd better relight the fire in a hurry!

00:15:13.760 --> 00:15:15.940
Flammable, flammable...

00:15:17.960 --> 00:15:20.550
I have to hurry and get them to notice!

00:15:20.550 --> 00:15:22.240
Hurry, hurry...

00:15:47.700 --> 00:15:48.640
This way!

00:15:49.010 --> 00:15:50.290
That must be the ship.

00:15:50.290 --> 00:15:51.410
Hey!

00:15:51.410 --> 00:15:53.660
Hey, right here!

00:16:13.650 --> 00:16:15.380
--Right here!
--This way!

00:16:45.940 --> 00:16:47.700
The rescue ship came for us!

00:16:47.960 --> 00:16:49.950
But it's behaving strangely.

00:17:10.310 --> 00:17:11.700
What should we do, Luna?

00:17:12.450 --> 00:17:15.640
Like we decided, we'll return to Everyone's House for now.

00:17:16.240 --> 00:17:17.030
I guess so.

00:17:32.700 --> 00:17:34.050
Over there.

00:17:45.980 --> 00:17:46.910
Welcome back.

00:17:47.180 --> 00:17:48.340
You're late.

00:17:49.090 --> 00:17:51.830
I went to the beach to check on the rescue ship.

00:17:53.210 --> 00:17:54.410
Is the ship okay?

00:17:57.040 --> 00:17:59.210
It crash-landed on the water a long distance out.

00:17:59.780 --> 00:18:02.890
Crash-landed? Then they really did have some sort of trouble?

00:18:03.300 --> 00:18:03.980
Probably.

00:18:04.690 --> 00:18:07.610
That low flying can't have been normal.

00:18:08.030 --> 00:18:09.980
And it flew like it had lost its balance.

00:18:10.540 --> 00:18:16.050
And we saw something like an escape capsule come out of the rescue ship.

00:18:16.280 --> 00:18:22.310
Really. I didn't notice, but in the meantime we should set up a signal on the beach.

00:18:22.610 --> 00:18:25.050
Luna, let's hurry to the western beach.

00:18:25.500 --> 00:18:26.100
Yes.

00:18:26.630 --> 00:18:28.160
What about Shingo and them?

00:18:28.460 --> 00:18:29.590
I'll go call them back.

00:18:30.080 --> 00:18:32.550
Everyone else, go on ahead to the western beach.

00:18:33.710 --> 00:18:34.580
Please do.

00:18:43.540 --> 00:18:46.500
But that rescue ship was awfully big.

00:18:46.760 --> 00:18:49.050
Based on the shape, I'd say it was a transport ship.

00:18:49.540 --> 00:18:52.580
Why would a transport ship come to rescue us?

00:18:52.800 --> 00:18:56.780
It probably just picked up our distress signal in mid-voyage.

00:18:56.960 --> 00:18:59.250
But I wonder where it came from.

00:18:59.590 --> 00:19:02.480
I didn't think this planet has been found yet.

00:19:02.810 --> 00:19:04.910
Come to think of it, that's true...

00:19:05.250 --> 00:19:09.230
Maybe the transport ship was also swallowed up by the gravity storm.

00:19:10.950 --> 00:19:15.080
Because it's an undiscovered planet, they shouldn't have been able to come with warp navigation.

00:19:15.080 --> 00:19:19.760
We don't know that for sure. Maybe they found a new warp route.

00:19:19.760 --> 00:19:22.160
The voice on the radio was very calm.

00:19:22.730 --> 00:19:25.650
It didn't sound like they'd just been through a gravity storm.

00:19:27.900 --> 00:19:29.400
Anyways, we'd better hurry.

00:19:29.850 --> 00:19:30.560
Let's go.

00:19:42.980 --> 00:19:43.880
Welcome back.

00:19:44.100 --> 00:19:44.810
I'm back.

00:19:44.890 --> 00:19:45.600
Where's Luna?

00:19:45.600 --> 00:19:47.660
Sorry, she went on ahead.

00:19:49.500 --> 00:19:50.400
Luna...

00:19:50.850 --> 00:19:53.290
You're late! At such a critical time...

00:19:53.550 --> 00:19:55.540
Has there been any contact from them?

00:19:55.690 --> 00:19:57.600
Nothing at all.

00:19:57.980 --> 00:19:58.880
I see...

00:19:59.140 --> 00:19:59.960
Where's everyone?

00:20:00.340 --> 00:20:02.660
They're headed for the western beach.

00:20:03.490 --> 00:20:05.440
We have to go west after all...

00:20:05.660 --> 00:20:08.330
The rescue ship seems to have crash landed out at sea.

00:20:08.330 --> 00:20:11.510
Just like I thought! We're all ready.

00:20:13.240 --> 00:20:14.290
Let's go!

00:20:30.040 --> 00:20:30.830
There it is.

00:20:52.950 --> 00:20:58.350
Luna!

00:20:58.350 --> 00:21:00.040
Adam! Everyone!

00:21:00.790 --> 00:21:01.690
Luna!

00:21:05.100 --> 00:21:05.810
Luna...

00:21:05.810 --> 00:21:07.160
Were you okay?

00:21:11.290 --> 00:21:12.450
There's a light!

00:21:12.980 --> 00:21:14.780
That's the rescue ship?

00:21:14.960 --> 00:21:16.090
It's okay.

00:21:16.310 --> 00:21:18.190
The rescue ship is okay!

00:21:18.380 --> 00:21:20.400
Hey! Over here!

00:21:20.400 --> 00:21:21.640
Please help us!

00:21:23.700 --> 00:21:26.100
It's pointless. They can't hear you at this distance.

00:21:26.890 --> 00:21:28.610
Has there been any response?

00:21:28.990 --> 00:21:29.780
Well...

00:21:30.340 --> 00:21:34.650
We've had a fire burning ever since we got here, but there's been nothing.

00:21:34.880 --> 00:21:36.940
We should burn the fire even brighter.

00:21:37.580 --> 00:21:40.430
If we do, there should be some sort of response.

00:21:42.450 --> 00:21:45.260
Burn, burn! Burn bright!

00:21:46.090 --> 00:21:49.460
I hope the rescue ship notices this.

00:22:05.060 --> 00:22:07.160
It's almost like a welcoming fire.

00:22:07.800 --> 00:22:08.780
Welcoming fire?

00:22:09.490 --> 00:22:12.410
Yes. I was in a book I read a long time ago.

00:22:12.940 --> 00:22:15.490
A fire burned to welcome back spirits.

00:22:15.640 --> 00:22:16.880
Spirits...

00:22:17.660 --> 00:22:21.150
I don't care if they're ghosts or anything else, as long as they come to help us.

00:22:23.210 --> 00:22:26.140
But I wonder why they ain't comin'.

00:22:26.140 --> 00:22:29.780
Say or do something! Hey!

00:22:30.530 --> 00:22:33.560
Maybe they can't move, and are stuck where they crash landed.

00:22:34.090 --> 00:22:36.900
So maybe they're repairing something somewhere?

00:22:36.900 --> 00:22:37.880
Perhaps...

00:22:41.060 --> 00:22:43.910
I'm sure they'll come help us soon.

00:22:44.100 --> 00:22:47.210
Yes. In the meantime, we'll just wait.

00:23:03.640 --> 00:23:07.200
When this storm clears, the rescue ship will come save us!

00:23:07.390 --> 00:23:09.110
Luna! It's serious!

00:23:09.300 --> 00:23:11.140
An old man washed ashore alone!

00:23:11.330 --> 00:23:12.680
Kaoru found him!

00:23:13.650 --> 00:23:15.640
Mister, snap out of it!

00:23:15.830 --> 00:23:16.880
What happened?

00:23:17.180 --> 00:23:20.480
Just what happened inside that rescue ship?

00:23:20.930 --> 00:23:23.810
I smell somethin' dangerous...

00:23:25.540 --> 00:23:28.090
Next time: Tenacious bunch
